LAST-MODIFIED:20260726T095445Z
SEQUENCE:1785059685
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260727
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260728
SUMMARY:Full-Body Athletic Strength
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3500 kcal\, 180 g protein\, 505 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protei
 n in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again af
 ter.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Temporary 50% work
 ing-load cap.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 7 min easy cardio\, squat-to-stand\, band pu
 ll-aparts\, push-ups\, and hinge ramp sets.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression:
  double progression\; add load only when presses\, hinges\, and pulls are
  all stable at RPE 6-7 or lower. Prior-month recovery feedback: reduce on
 e back-off set and cap all compounds at RPE 6-7. Lower-body feedback: tri
 m one lower-body set\, stay 1-3 RIR\, and swap to the safest machine or u
 nilateral pattern if joints or back flare. Prior-month recovery feedback:
  reduce one back-off set and cap all compounds at RPE 6-7. Temporary low-
 back recovery constraint: cap loaded work at RPE 6-7 and stop if symptoms
  rise. Return-to-impact ramp: progress only when symptoms stay 0-2/10 and
  the next morning is not worse.\n- Incline press\, shoulder press\, or be
 nch press: top set 1 x 6-8 at RPE 6-7\, then 2-3 back-off sets x 8-10 at 
 RPE 6-7.\n- Back-friendly posterior chain: seated or lying leg curl 3 x 1
 0-15 at RPE 6-7\, plus bodyweight glute bridge 2 x 12 if symptom-free.\n-
  Pull-ups or chest-supported rows: 4 x 6-10 at RPE 6-7 paired with front-
 foot elevated split squat or hack squat 3 x 8-10 per leg at RPE 6-7.\n- S
 houlder\, trap\, and quad finisher: lateral raises 2-3 x 15-20\, dumbbell
  trap raise 2 x 12-15\, leg extension 2 x 12-15\, then weighted sit-ups 2
  x 8-12. Temporary low-back recovery constraint: avoid loaded hinging and
  max-brace loading\; use machines or supported positions where possible.\
 n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place ca
 rbohydrates before and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays
  22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
