SUMMARY:Core + Chest/Back Strength Capacity
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 175 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 35-45 g protein in 4 meals\, 40-70 g carbs before 
 lifting\, and a protein-plus-carb meal after training.\nCategory: gym\nRu
 n volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Temporary 50% working-load cap.\n\nWarm-U
 p:\n- 5 min easy bike\, shoulder prep\, thoracic mobility\, hip openers\,
  and two light press/row ramp sets.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: this is
  the eighth strength day in the 14-day wave\; cap work at RPE 6-7\, use s
 upersets\, and trim accessories before anchor work if recovery dips. Temp
 orary low-back recovery constraint: cap loaded work at RPE 6-7 and stop i
 f symptoms rise. Return-to-impact ramp: progress only when symptoms stay 
 0-2/10 and the next morning is not worse.\n- Chest volume: bench press 3 
 x 6-8\, incline dumbbell press 3 x 8-10\, dumbbell press 2 x 8-10\, pec-d
 eck 2 x 12-15\, dips 2 x 6-10\, and push-ups 2 x clean reps.\n- Back volu
 me: lat pulldown or pull-ups 3 x 8-12\, cable row or chest-supported row 
 3 x 8-12\, face pulls 2 x 12-15\, and rear delt fly or reverse pec-deck 2
  x 15-20.\n- Leg maintenance: hip thrust or glute bridge 3 x 8-12\, leg e
 xtension 2 x 12-15\, and seated or lying hamstring curl 2 x 10-15 at RPE 
 7.\n- Core volume: Pallof press 3 x 10 per side\, side plank 2 x 30 sec p
 er side\, plank variations 2 x 30-45 sec\, hanging leg raises 2-3 sets\, 
 weighted sit-ups 2 x 8-12\, and kettlebell side bend or around the head k
 ettlebell 2 x 10. Arm top-up: tricep pulldown 2 x 10-15\, preacher curls 
 2 x 10-15\, and reverse curls 2 x 12-15. Temporary low-back recovery cons
 traint: avoid loaded hinging and max-brace loading\; use machines or supp
 orted positions where possible.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep pr
 otein near target\, and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\
 nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints fee
 l stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
