DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3500 kcal\, 180 g protein\, 505 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protei
 n in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again af
 ter.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Temporary 50% work
 ing-load cap.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 7 min easy cardio\, squat-to-stand\, band pu
 ll-aparts\, push-ups\, and hinge ramp sets.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression:
  double progression\; add load only when presses\, hinges\, and pulls are
  all stable at RPE 8 or lower. Prior-month recovery feedback: reduce one 
 back-off set and cap all compounds at RPE 7-8. Lower-body feedback: trim 
 one lower-body set\, stay 1-3 RIR\, and swap to the safest machine or uni
 lateral pattern if joints or back flare. Prior-month recovery feedback: r
 educe one back-off set and cap all compounds at RPE 7-8. Low-back ramp: s
 tart lightly and add load only when the next morning is symptom-free. Ret
 urn-to-impact ramp: progress only when symptoms stay 0-2/10 and the next 
 morning is not worse.\n- Incline press\, shoulder press\, or bench press:
  top set 1 x 6-8 at RPE 8\, then 2-3 back-off sets x 8-10 at RPE 7-8.\n- 
 Back-friendly posterior chain: hip thrust\, glute bridge\, or leg curl 3 
 x 8-12 at RPE 6-7\; skip loaded hinges and back-extension work\; start li
 ghtly.\n- Pull-ups or chest-supported rows: 4 x 6-10 at RPE 8 paired with
  front-foot elevated split squat or hack squat 3 x 8-10 per leg at RPE 8.
 \n- Shoulder\, trap\, and quad finisher: lateral raises 2-3 x 15-20\, dum
 bbell trap raise 2 x 12-15\, leg extension 2 x 12-15\, then weighted sit-
 ups 2 x 8-12. Low-back ramp: skip loaded hinges and back-extension work\;
  start lightly and keep supported posterior-chain work pain-free.\n\nFuel
 ing:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydr
 ates before and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-
 06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
